# Authorship & attribution

- Never add `Co-authored-by` (or any AI/tool co-author trailer) to commits.
- Never leave agent/AI metadata in the repo: no “Generated by…”, Cursor/Copilot badges, assistant credits in README, commit messages, file headers, or docs.
- Commits and project history should read as the user’s / team’s work only.

# Code style

- Prefer simple, clean, readable code over clever or heavily abstracted designs.
- Add short comments where intent is not obvious (why a GPS interval is 3–5s, what a tripwire means, RLS intent) — not noise on every line.
- Keep the file tree shallow and obvious: few folders, clear names, no deep nesting or “enterprise” layering until something actually needs it.
- Avoid premature packages, factories, DI, or micro-abstractions. One module ≈ one job.
- When scaffolding: small working stubs with clear comments beat large empty framework shells.
